{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "purpose": "simulation Phase 4c (#841): sm.setnoise(mode='tsys-atm') scenarios, run by CASA and by casa-rs",
  "notes": [
    "Each noisy scenario's noise is its DATA minus its noise-free twin's. A tsys-atm term's sigma differs by row and channel, so compare_sm_ms.py divides each implementation's noise by the sigma of CASA's AtmosCorruptor formula with ATM through casatools' at tool (tsys_atm_sigma, each antenna's elevation of the field at the row's TIME), at the frequencies each implementation gives ATM: CASA's grid from REF_FREQUENCY, half a band below each channel, and casa-rs's CHAN_FREQ (docs/CASA (C++) bugs.md). Each normalized noise must have unit variance per correlation and class within five standard errors, and a KS test compares the two.",
    "atm-lines has two windows of 32 channels of 100 MHz across the 183.31 GHz and 325.15 GHz water lines, where the two frequency mappings give noise of very different variance, dishes of 12 m and 7 m, autocorrelations, and every site and receiver parameter away from its default.",
    "atm-narrow has two windows of 32 narrow channels at 100 GHz and 230 GHz, where half a band moves Tsys by under 1e-4, so CASA's and casa-rs's variances are also compared directly in groups of rows (direct_spws: spectral window, dish pair, auto or cross, time bin), with the site's and pwv's defaults.",
    "The field transits near the zenith at ALMA, and the scans keep above 50 degrees elevation, where CASA's 100 s airmass cache moves Tsys by under 0.1 % (docs/CASA (C++) bugs.md). Each scenario has one integration time."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
